From ed235b8bf715a45f89feddc19ad06c612b60dd08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:22:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Hold an early ConnectLink until the child GBA has seen the
 handshake

When the adapter stands in for the parent (the GBA's seat is not 0), a
ConnectLink that arrives before the adapter has sent any 0xB9A0 switches the
handshake straight from 0xD15E to 0x8FFF. UsbSection::establishConncection()
then waits for isHandshakeEnabled(), "the last word sent was 0xB9A0", which
never becomes true: the link hangs before LinkConnected. It also hangs when
0xB9A0 was sent for less than the 50 ms poll interval before 0x8FFF replaced
it, and the GBA is sent 0x8FFF without having seen the handshake.

The host apps avoid it with a delay: the netplay bridge waits 150 ms
(CONNECT_GRACE_MS), Celio-Client's cable page 150 ms, gen3-poke-multiplayer
350 ms. Celio-Client's local multi-adapter session has none: it sends
ConnectLink to the other adapters as soon as seat 0 reports LinkConnected,
about one handshake round after StartHandshake, which is inside the window.

ConnectLink is now held until eight 0xB9A0 rounds have gone out (about the
bridge's measured 150 ms), then sent at once. A ConnectLink that comes later
behaves as before.

tests/host/handshakeTest.cpp runs the real PacketLayer and UsbSection
against a modelled GBA, over host stand-ins for the Zephyr calls they use,
with ConnectLink 0, 5, 30, 60 and 200 ms after StartHandshake (seat 1 of 2),
0 ms in seat 2 of 4, and seat 0 of 2. Before this change the 0, 5 and 30 ms
cases and the 4-player case hang (eight failed checks); after it every case
connects, and the GBA sees eight 0xB9A0 before 0x8FFF. Also clean under
ASan and UBSan. Not built with Zephyr or run on RP2040 hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014LvpUYFw94JkaNFyrbwJmK
